\begin_layout Standard
We define the slope of v-t graph as a, so it gives 
\begin_inset Formula $a=\dfrac{v-v_{o}}{t}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Manipulating the form of this equation, we get 
\begin_inset Formula $v=v_{o}+at$
\end_inset

 , which is newton's first equation of motion in scalar form.
\end_layout

